<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Athaliah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 835 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Athaliah was queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judah">Judah</a> for about six years in the 9th century BCE, the only woman to rule either <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a> kingdom in her own right. A daughter of the house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/omri">Omri</a>, she married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jehoram-of-judah">Jehoram of Judah</a>, and after her son Ahaziah was killed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jehu">Jehu</a>'s coup she seized power and killed most of the royal family. The priest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jehoiada">Jehoiada</a> overthrew and killed her, placing her grandson Joash on the throne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/athaliah.jpg" alt="Athaliah" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Guillaume Rouille · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Athalia.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
